      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Snow White and the Huntsman** (2012) marks a gritty reimagining of the classic fairy tale, following the darker revision trend started by **Pan's Labyrinth** (2006) and **Alice in Wonderland** (2010). Charlize Theron's terrifying Queen Ravenna elevates the film beyond typical fantasy fare, channeling the menacing presence of Angelica Huston in **The Witches** (1990). The film's visual aesthetic borrows heavily from **Lord of the Rings** (2001-2003), particularly in its sweeping landscape shots and medieval warfare sequences."
      },
